From gordon at chronitis.net  Mon Jul 22 09:52:02 2019
From: gordon at chronitis.net (Gordon Ball)
Date: Mon, 22 Jul 2019 08:52:02 +0000
Subject: [R-pkg-team] Bug#932179: (no subject)
References: <156327546315.20465.5512696571984369015.reportbug@sputnik.fam-tille.de>
Message-ID: <20190722085202.tqvyscbn5go6qweq@emissary.chronitis.net>

I think supporting this mechanism in dh-update-R should be fairly easy,
so it's really a policy question of what an appropriate compat level and
compat-mechanism is preferred for R packaging.

Debhelper 12 is available in buster, stretch-backports (and
bionic-backports or later ubuntu). My inclination is that it is cleaner
to not have the d/compat file and just have it inline in d/control.

I'll see if I can come up with a patch for dh-update-R which supports
this mechanism. After that we can decide if it should be made the
default for new and/or updated packages.


